The '''1998 United States Senate election in Oregon''' was held on November 3, 1998. Incumbent [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] U.S. Senator [[Ron Wyden]] won re-election to his first full term, defeating Republican nominee [[John Lim]], a state senator in a landslide (Lim only carried [[Malheur County, Oregon|Malheur County]]). As of 2022, this is the last time [[Grant County, Oregon|Grant County]] and [[Harney County, Oregon|Harney County]] have supported a Democrat in a U.S. Senate election.

==Democratic nomination==
* John Sweeney, retired city parks worker
* [[Ron Wyden]], incumbent U.S. Senator

